  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Ruth, I found the problem. Yesterday's agent promised you a $6.50 account credit for the missing garlic knots on order Q-7690, but it was never applied. I've now added the $6.50 credit to your account. You can use it on a future order.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thanks for finding that. I'm fairly sure the agent said $10, though, not $6.50. I don't have the chat from yesterday in front of me, so I can't check it exactly. Could you look again and see whether the promise was $10? If the record really says $6.50, I'll go with that, but I wanted to make sure."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I checked again, and the record says $6.50. The ticket (TK-881, created yesterday at 8:15 PM) shows the agent promised $6.50 in account credit for the missing garlic knots. That's also the price of the garlic knots on the order. I can only issue what the record shows, so $6.50 is the amount I can honor. It's already on your account.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, if the record says $6.50, then I'll accept that. I was going by memory, and I'd rather be sure than argue about it. Thank you for checking and for adding it to my account.\n\nIs there anything else I need to do to use the credit on my next order, or will it apply automatically?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're welcome, Ruth. I can't see how credit gets applied at checkout, so I can't say for sure whether it's automatic. Your account balance now shows $6.50, and the credit is meant for future orders. At checkout, look for a credit or balance line. If you don't see it, contact us again and we'll look into it.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with today?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thanks, that's clear enough. I'll check at checkout on my next order, and if the credit doesn't show up I'll reach out again.\n\nI think that takes care of it for today. Thank you for your help."
  }
